# UI conventions

- Read root `AGENTS.md` and consult installed Next.js documentation for framework changes.
- Keep product copy direct and operational in Mozambican Portuguese (`pt-MZ`). Localize display labels without changing API enum values.
- Put routes in App Router pages, domain components in `components/`, primitives in `components/ui/`, shell in `components/shell/`, and requests in `lib/api-client.ts`.
- Prefer server components. Preserve accessible loading/empty/error states, dense full-width data presentation, neutral structural colors, and restrained brand/destructive colors.
- Avoid exposing internal acronyms, implementation details, or legal citations in visible or accessible text.
- Coordinate UI types and client changes with `packages/api-clients` and contract tests.
